@startuml sd20_release_retire
!include ../style.iuml
title SD-20 Release and retire trains (UC-20)
autonumber

box "CTC Office process" #F7F9FC
participant "StubCtcOffice" as Model
participant "TrainTracker" as Tr
end box
participant "Central Harness\n(roster)" as H
participant "Train Model and\nthe line's Train Controller" as TM

== Release (step n) ==
loop each line, waiting trains most behind schedule first
  alt a released train on the line is not yet on the track
    Model -> Model : skip the line (one at a time)
  else line not ready, or yard exit block occupied, closed,\nclosing or within a train's authority, or the scheduler\nholds the run
    Model -> Model : the train keeps waiting
  else
    Model -> Model : release it: it holds the yard exit block\n(Green 63, Red 9)
  end
end
Model --> H : new_trains = [NewTrain(train_id, line)]\n(once, on this step only)
H -> TM : add the train at the yard exit block

== Leaving the yard (a later step) ==
H -> Model : step (yard exit block now occupied)
Model -> Tr : update(..., waiting = released trains)
Tr --> Model : the released train is on the track
Model -> Model : it gets suggestions from now on (SD-21)

== Retire (step m) ==
loop each train sent to the yard
  opt its head and tail are in the yard entry block\n(Green 57, Red 9), its authority there is 0\nand it can no longer be moving
    Model -> Model : drop its order; out of service
  end
end
Model --> H : retired_trains = [RetiredTrain(train_id)]
H -> TM : remove the train
H -> Model : (next step) the yard entry block is clear
Model -> Model : a scheduled run is "done"
@enduml
